<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">

<head>
    <%- include('partials/head') %>
</head>

<body>

    <!-- ===== NAVBAR ===== -->
    <%- include('partials/navbar') %>

        <%# M12.P1-R8 — Pilot privacy notice.

            Every statement here is grounded in the shipped implementation:
              - collected fields        -> database/schema.sql, database/supabase/0001,
                                           controllers/authController.js
              - Google scopes           -> controllers/authController.js ('openid email profile')
              - session record/cookie   -> config/sessionConfig.js, services/*SessionStore.js
              - security logging        -> services/auditService.js, middleware/roleAuth.js (R5),
                                           middleware/logger.js (path only, never query strings)
              - rate-limit storage      -> services/rateLimitStore.js (HMAC digest + integer only)
              - media delivery          -> config/cloudinary.js, utils/mediaUrl.js

            Deliberately NOT claimed: any consent or legal-basis characterisation,
            any automatic/scheduled deletion, and any assertion about whether data
            is or is not shared onward. Retention below is an owner-managed manual
            commitment, described as such. %>

        <main class="legal page-transition" id="privacyMain">
            <style nonce="<%= cspNonce %>">
                .legal {
                    max-width: 900px;
                    margin: 0 auto;
                    padding: 7rem 1.25rem 4rem;
                }

                .legal__title {
                    font-size: clamp(1.75rem, 4vw, 2.5rem);
                    margin: 0 0 0.5rem;
                }

                .legal__updated {
                    color: var(--gray-500, #6b7280);
                    margin: 0 0 2rem;
                    font-size: 0.95rem;
                }

                .legal h2 {
                    font-size: clamp(1.15rem, 2.5vw, 1.4rem);
                    margin: 2.25rem 0 0.75rem;
                    padding-bottom: 0.4rem;
                    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border, #e5e7eb);
                }

                .legal h3 {
                    font-size: 1.05rem;
                    margin: 1.5rem 0 0.5rem;
                }

                .legal p,
                .legal li {
                    line-height: 1.7;
                }

                .legal ul {
                    padding-left: 1.4rem;
                    margin: 0.5rem 0 1rem;
                }

                .legal li {
                    margin-bottom: 0.4rem;
                }

                .legal__callout {
                    border: 1px solid var(--border, #e5e7eb);
                    border-left: 3px solid var(--gold, #c8a24a);
                    border-radius: 6px;
                    padding: 0.9rem 1.1rem;
                    margin: 1.25rem 0;
                }

                .legal__table-wrap {
                    overflow-x: auto;
                    margin: 0.75rem 0 1.25rem;
                }

                .legal table {
                    width: 100%;
                    border-collapse: collapse;
                    min-width: 520px;
                }

                .legal th,
                .legal td {
                    border: 1px solid var(--border, #e5e7eb);
                    padding: 0.6rem 0.7rem;
                    text-align: left;
                    vertical-align: top;
                    font-size: 0.95rem;
                }

                .legal th {
                    font-weight: 600;
                }

                .legal a {
                    text-decoration: underline;
                }

                @media (max-width: 640px) {
                    .legal {
                        padding-top: 5.5rem;
                    }
                }
            </style>

            <h1 class="legal__title">Privacy Notice</h1>
            <p class="legal__updated">
                CampuSphere — CSPC Virtual Campus Map Tour. Last updated 29 July 2026.
            </p>

            <div class="legal__callout">
                <p>
                    <strong>CampuSphere is a student capstone project, not an official
                        Camarines Sur Polytechnic Colleges (CSPC) system.</strong>
                    It is built and operated by <strong>Team Dutchess</strong>, a student
                    group at CSPC, and is currently running as a limited, facilitator-guided
                    pilot for evaluation purposes only. It is not a student records system,
                    not an enrolment system, and not a source of official CSPC information.
                </p>
            </div>

            <h2 id="what-we-collect">1. What CampuSphere collects</h2>

            <p>
                CampuSphere collects only what it needs to sign you in, show you the
                role-appropriate parts of the campus tour, and keep the pilot secure.
            </p>

            <h3>Identity and account details</h3>
            <ul>
                <li>Your full name and email address.</li>
                <li>A username derived from your account details.</li>
                <li>
                    Your role, which the application assigns automatically from your
                    email domain when you sign in with Google:
                    <code>@my.cspc.edu.ph</code> becomes <em>student</em>,
                    <code>@cspc.edu.ph</code> becomes <em>instructor</em>, and
                    <code>@gmail.com</code> becomes <em>guest</em>.
                </li>
            </ul>

            <h3>Role-specific profile details</h3>
            <ul>
                <li><strong>Students:</strong> student ID number, course, year level, and semester.</li>
                <li><strong>Instructors:</strong> employee ID, position, and department.</li>
                <li><strong>Guests:</strong> address and phone number.</li>
            </ul>

            <h3>Authentication details</h3>
            <ul>
                <li>
                    If you sign in with Google, CampuSphere requests only the
                    <code>openid</code>, <code>email</code>, and <code>profile</code>
                    scopes, and stores a Google account identifier alongside your
                    verified email address. <strong>CampuSphere never receives or
                        stores your Google password.</strong>
                </li>
                <li>
                    If you register with an email address and password, only a bcrypt
                    hash of that password is stored. The password itself is never
                    written to the database or to any log.
                </li>
            </ul>

            <h3>Session details</h3>
            <ul>
                <li>
                    A server-side session record containing a session identifier, an
                    expiry time, and your signed-in account details.
                </li>
                <li>
                    One session cookie in your browser. In production it is named
                    <code>__Host-campusphere.sid</code> and is set
                    <code>HttpOnly</code>, <code>Secure</code>, and
                    <code>SameSite=Lax</code>, so it is not readable by page scripts.
                </li>
            </ul>

            <h3>Security and integrity details</h3>
            <ul>
                <li>
                    Sign-in attempts are recorded, including the email address that was
                    submitted. A failed sign-in never records the submitted password.
                </li>
                <li>
                    When a signed-in account requests something its role is not allowed
                    to access, CampuSphere records the account identifier, the role, and
                    the requested path. Requests from signed-out visitors are
                    <strong>not</strong> recorded.
                </li>
                <li>
                    Server request logs record only the HTTP method and the path. Query
                    strings are deliberately stripped, so search terms and sign-in codes
                    do not reach the logs.
                </li>
                <li>
                    Abuse-prevention counters store only a keyed cryptographic digest and
                    a number. They do not store your IP address, email address, or account
                    identifier in a readable form.
                </li>
            </ul>

            <h2 id="why">2. Why CampuSphere uses this information</h2>
            <ul>
                <li><strong>Authentication</strong> — to sign you in and keep you signed in.</li>
                <li><strong>Authorization</strong> — to show each role only the pages it should see.</li>
                <li><strong>Routing</strong> — to generate walking routes between campus buildings.</li>
                <li><strong>Schedules</strong> — to display room and facility schedules published by an administrator.</li>
                <li><strong>Virtual tour (VR)</strong> — to show 360° panoramas and guided arrival states.</li>
                <li><strong>Pilot evaluation</strong> — to check that the application behaves correctly during the pilot.</li>
            </ul>

            <h2 id="services">3. Services CampuSphere runs on</h2>

            <p>
                CampuSphere is a student project built on external platforms. Running the
                application necessarily means your information is handled by the services
                below, each of which operates under its own privacy terms.
            </p>

            <div class="legal__table-wrap">
                <table>
                    <caption class="sr-only">Third-party services CampuSphere depends on and their role</caption>
                    <thead>
                        <tr>
                            <th scope="col">Service</th>
                            <th scope="col">Role in CampuSphere</th>
                        </tr>
                    </thead>
                    <tbody>
                        <tr>
                            <th scope="row">Vercel</th>
                            <td>Hosts and serves the application.</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <th scope="row">Supabase</th>
                            <td>Stores the application database, including accounts, profiles, and session records.</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <th scope="row">Upstash</th>
                            <td>Stores abuse-prevention counters (keyed digests and numbers only).</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <th scope="row">Google (Sign in with Google)</th>
                            <td>Verifies your identity when you choose to sign in with Google. CampuSphere requests
                                only <code>openid</code>, <code>email</code>, and <code>profile</code>.</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <th scope="row">Cloudinary</th>
                            <td>Delivers campus photographs and 360° panorama images. These are pictures of buildings
                                and grounds, not personal data about you.</td>
                        </tr>
                    </tbody>
                </table>
            </div>

            <h2 id="feedback">4. Pilot feedback is collected separately</h2>
            <p>
                Pilot feedback is gathered through a <strong>separate Google Form created
                    by the project owner</strong>. That form is not part of this
                application. <strong>CampuSphere does not receive, store, or display any
                    feedback response</strong> — the application has no feedback table, no
                feedback API, and no feedback screen. Anything you submit in that form is
                handled by Google Forms under the form's own settings and Google's terms.
            </p>

            <h2 id="retention">5. How long information is kept</h2>
            <p>
                Pilot data is intended to be kept until <strong>30 days after Team
                    Dutchess's final capstone defense</strong>. After that period, the
                project owner will <strong>manually delete</strong> the pilot accounts,
                profiles, and session records, unless CSPC requires them to be retained
                for longer.
            </p>
            <div class="legal__callout">
                <p>
                    <strong>This deletion is a manual, owner-managed step.</strong>
                    CampuSphere does not run any automatic or scheduled deletion job, and
                    this notice does not promise one. Expired session records are the one
                    exception: the session store removes them as part of normal operation.
                </p>
            </div>

            <h2 id="rights">6. Your rights</h2>
            <p>
                Under the Philippine Data Privacy Act of 2012 (Republic Act No. 10173),
                you have rights over your personal information, including the rights to be
                informed, to access it, to have inaccurate entries corrected, to object to
                its processing, and to request its erasure or blocking.
            </p>
            <p>
                To exercise any of these rights during the pilot, you may:
            </p>
            <ul>
                <li>
                    speak to the <strong>pilot facilitator</strong> running your session,
                    who can pass the request to Team Dutchess; or
                </li>
                <li>
                    contact the <strong>CSPC Data Protection Officer</strong> through the
                    official contact details published with the college's privacy policy
                    (linked below).
                </li>
            </ul>
            <p>
                You can also simply ask a facilitator not to create an account for you.
                Taking part in the pilot is voluntary.
            </p>

            <h2 id="cspc-policy">7. CSPC's official privacy policy</h2>
            <p>
                CampuSphere is a student project and this notice covers the pilot
                application only. Camarines Sur Polytechnic Colleges publishes its own
                institutional privacy policy, which governs the college's own systems and
                contains the official Data Protection Officer contact details:
            </p>
            <p>
                <a href="https://cspc.edu.ph/governance/privacy-policy/" rel="noopener noreferrer"
                    target="_blank">https://cspc.edu.ph/governance/privacy-policy/</a>
            </p>

            <p style="margin-top:2.5rem;">
                <a href="/">← Back to Home</a>
            </p>
        </main>

        <%- include('partials/footer') %>

            <%- include('partials/theme-toggle') %>
</body>

</html>
